    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This Open-File Report is in response to requests for my programs for simulating ground motions from earthquakes. The programs are based on modifications I have made to the stochastic model first introduced by Hanks and McGuire (1981). The report contains source codes, written in Fortran, and executables that can be used on a PC. Programs are included both for time-domain and for random-vibration simulations. In addition, programs are included to produce Fourier amplitude spectra for the models used in the simulations and to convert shear velocity vs. depth into frequency-dependent amplification. The report contains an improvement in the implementation of the random vibration method not published before.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
